+     * <p>The normal radio-off path is also used for airplane mode and waits for data on every
+     * phone to disconnect before powering down the modem. On legacy DSDS devices where a physical
+     * SIM switch is implemented as per-phone radio power, waiting for the other phone's active
+     * default data network can only end at the global timeout. Tear down this phone's data and let
+     * the modem finish the local cleanup instead.</p>
